=== CONFLICTS ===
# ARCH E-5 (#1521) PARTIALLY fixed #1223 — the NO-IMPORT case only.
# compiler/tools/test_cmd.mdk's single-file drivers now compute
# `canonicalPathId` (last-containing-root, round-trip-guarded) instead of a
# hardcoded "__user__" literal, via the EXPORTED `singleRootId`. This probe's
# `single` arm CALLS that same exported function directly (not by reusing the
# graph arm's `mid` as its elaboration id, which would manufacture AGREE and
# prove nothing — see singleArm's own comment) — so a genuine single~graph
# CONFLICT is still REACHABLE here, and the DRIVER regressing back to plain
# `moduleIdOfPath` inside `singleRootId` would flip this gate red.
# ⚠️ THE ROOTS LIST FED TO `singleRootId` IS STILL THIS ARM'S OWN MODEL of
# `testFilesGo` (`entrySearchRoots (dirOf path) ++ [stdlibDir]`), not a call
# to it — see `singleArm`'s comment for what that residual gap covers.
# The rows #1223 pinned (single-root corpus) read AGREE, and a nested-project
# row (test/origin_fixtures/nested) requires the last-root convention to
# agree, REGARDLESS of directory nesting (that fixture is cross-directory).
# #1223 stays OPEN: an IMPORT-BEARING file's ENTRY-vs-DEPENDENCY id asymmetry
# (loader.mdk:662-669, never touched by this fix) still reproduces — pinned in
# this gate's dedicated entry_residual section, not this table.
